    "q-68936": {
      "dom_id": "step-q68936",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Nathan, a freelance journalist, charges $$0.04$ per word for his financial articles. How many words would it take for him to earn $1$ dollar?",
      "worked_solution": "We are given the unit rate of $$0.04$ per word (dollars per word). To find how many words  it would take for him to earn $1$ dollar we need to find the unit rate in words per dollar. So, we take the reciprocal: \n\n$$\n0.04\\,\\text{dollars per word}\\,\\to \\,1÷0.04=25\\,\\text{words per dollar}\n$$\n\nSo, the unit rate is $25$ words per dollar. Therefore, Nathan writes $25$ words for $1$ dollar.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
