    "q-91920": {
      "dom_id": "step-q91920",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Louis visits a snack shop, the unit price for nuts is $$8$ per pound. How many pounds of nuts can Louis buy for $$1?$",
      "worked_solution": "We are given the unit rate of $$8$ per pound (dollars per pound). To find how many pounds of nuts she can buy for  $$1,$ we need to find the unit rate in pounds per dollar. So, we take the reciprocal: \n\n$$\n8\\,\\text{dollars per pound}\\,\\to \\,1÷8=0.125\\,\\text{pounds per dollar}\n$$\n\nSo, the unit rate is $0.125$ pounds per dollar. Therefore, Louis can buy $0.125$ pounds of nuts for $1$ dollar.",
